      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** 1700 mg three times daily = 5100 mg/day\n- **Typical maximum for immediate-release metformin:** 2550 mg/day (about 850 mg three times daily). Extended-release is usually capped at 2000 mg/day.\n- **Patient factors:** Normal renal and hepatic function and a 70 kg adult don't raise the limit. The 5100 mg/day dose is about double the maximum, which risks lactic acidosis and gastrointestinal toxicity.\n\nThis may be a transcription error, such as 850 mg or 1700 mg total daily dose. A licensed prescriber needs to confirm the intended drug, dose, and frequency before anything is entered. Please contact the medicine team or the prescriber.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a dose within the usual range, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals, I can enter that order. I'd still want the prescriber to confirm the dose and frequency, since I'm working from your summary and not the chart."
      }
